Hi [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] apologies for the delay. In order to have a better understanding of the feature, could you please share a RFC and details of implementation?

Below my initial thoughts:

* From a *regulatory* point of view (SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION 499.68LIGHT PASSENGER TRANSPORT SERVICES AND VEHICLE HIRE SERVICES REGULATIONS), _I do not see a legal constraint to allow fleets and self-employed drivers to set their own prices in the app_. The feature needs to ensure that the fleets and self-employed drivers can comply with the information requirements to consumers:
**  The fees levied for the provision of light passenger transport services must be publicised;
** The passenger should be informed in advance of the precise amount of the fee for the ride and the fleet/self-employed driver cannot charge a fee which is higher than the declared fee unless the passenger increases the length of the booked ride. 
* From a *labour law* point of view _I do not see a high risk of this feature fulfilling any of the 8 reclassification criteria_ established in SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION 452.108EMPLOYMENT STATUSNATIONAL STANDARD ORDER 
** …when  considering the employment status of a person who is nominally self-employed and is prima facie not considered as an employee, it shall be presumed that there is an employment relationship … if *at least five of the following criteria* are satisfied in relation to the person performing the work:
*** (a) he depends on one single person for whom the service is  provided  for  at  least  75%  of  his  income  over  a period of one year;
*** (b) he  depends  on  the  person  for  whom  the  service  is provided to determine what work is to be done and where and how the assigned work is to be carried out; 
*** (c) he  performs  the  work  using  equipment,  tools  or materials provided by the person for whom the service is provided;
*** (d) he is subject to a working time schedule or minimum work periods established by the person for whom the service is provided; 
*** (e) he cannot sub-contract his work to other individuals to substitute himself when carrying out work;
*** (f) he  is  integrated  in  the  structure  of  the  production process,  the  work  organisation  or  the  company’s  or other organization’s hierarchy;
*** (g) the  person’s  activity  is  a  core  element  in  the organization and pursuit of the objectives of the person for whom the service is provided; and
*** (h) he carries out similar tasks to existing employees, or, in the case when work is outsourced, he performs tasks similar to those formerly undertaken by employees.

Thank you and let me know if you have questions.

