konstantin.kulikov: Hey, the client never defines the pricing for payment systems. The total flow for Google Pay works in this way:
1. Client opens Google Pay system flow;
2. The user selects a particular payment method in the GPay flow;
3. GPay returns transaction token to the client;
4. The client provides this token to the backend;
5. The backend invokes payment transactions in the payment provider using this token.

The payment request you are talking about is just metadata for GooglePay/ApplePay to configure the payment SDK screen, it has nothing to do with the transaction. For example, based on the GooglePay https://developers.google.com/pay/api/android/reference/request-objects#TransactionInfodocumentation> client provides the `totalPrice` field to the SDK, but if the provided `totalPrice` is different our backend will try to charge with this payment token, and the transaction will be declined.

