Hi [~accountid:712020:f72e650a-da39-47a2-9587-36404101929a] , please find below my comments. Please note that I may have not understood the exact intention of the Customer as it seems that the remarks were translated into English. What I may suggest is that the Customer provides its proposed changes in track changes in English in the Special Terms, however, please note that we do not want to implement any changes in them unless really required.

* It is requested to write the last date of the validity period in Article 1.1 of the special conditions. For example, the Special Terms are signed for an indefinite period, the Customer can refuse the Special Terms and Bolt services by applying in writing 7 (seven) calendar days in advance.

{color:#4c9aff}PK: No need to adjust article 1.1. Special Terms are applicable as long as the Agreement is not terminated in accordance with T&Cs.{color}

* Replace the word "Agreement" with the words "General Terms and Conditions" in articles 1.2 and 1.3 of the special conditions. At the same time, the appropriate correction should be made in the English sample.

{color:#4c9aff}PK: No need to adjust articles 1.2 and 1.3. Agreement is defined in T&Cs as T&Cs + Special Terms.{color}

* In Article 2.1 of the special conditions, the concept of "credit limit" and the procedure for using it are requested to be written in more detail. For example, the Credit limit is the limit assigned by Bolt to the Customer at the end of the month to pay the fares and service fees for the use of Bolt services by the User during the month. The credit limit will be increased by Bolt if the service fee amount exceeds the credit limit, the credit limit will be paid by Bolt to the User (persons added by the Customer to the corporate account belonging to the Customer in Bolt's control panel and who can use Bolt's services on behalf of the Customer) or deposit from the Customer not required.

{color:#4c9aff}PK: Ok, we can precise that the credit limit is for Bolt Services and Service Fee. I do not get this part “{color}{color:#4c9aff}_The credit limit will be increased by Bolt if the service fee amount exceeds the credit limit, the credit limit will be paid by Bolt to the User (persons added by the Customer to the corporate account belonging to the Customer in Bolt's control panel and who can use Bolt's services on behalf of the Customer) or deposit from the Customer not required_{color}{color:#4c9aff}.” On what occasion should we pay anything back, especially to the User?{color}

* Article 2.2 of the special conditions is requested to be written more clearly, For example, Bolt Business offers a Control Panel for the Customer, and in return for this, 15% (fifteen percent) of the amount (travel fee) to be paid by the User for the service used during the month charges a service fee. The cost of services used by Users on behalf of the Client (fare) is also paid by the Client to Bolt.

{color:#4c9aff}PK: T&Cs describe what a Service Fee is so I do not see any point in adding the proposed part.{color}

* In order to clarify the words "invoiced payment" in Article 2.3 of the special conditions, the following sentence can be added: "Invoiced payment" means the payment of the fare and service fee for the services used at the end of the month without receiving any deposit from the Customer.

{color:#4c9aff}PK: There is no “invoiced payment” in article 2.3 so I do not understand the intention of the proposed change.{color}

* The first sentence of article 2.4 of the special conditions is requested to be changed as follows: "The customer is provided with a statement, invoice and electronic statement for payments and calculated service fees for Bolt Services used by Users during the previous calendar month. The value of the Bolt services used by the user on behalf of the customer (travel fee) is confirmed by the transfer deed between the parties every month" Mr. Turaj, please note that the submission of an electronic receipt for payments is a requirement of the Tax Code of the Republic of Azerbaijan.

{color:#4c9aff}PK: We cannot agree that Bolt Services fee will be paid after it is accepted by the Customer. It is payable upon providing such services which will be visible for the Customer in the Business Portal. Additionally, it is obvious that Bolt is obliged to follow legal obligation resulting from the legal acts whether they are directly indicated in the agreement or not.{color}

* The first sentence of article 2.5 of the special conditions is requested to be changed in the following order: After the customer approves the act of handover and receives the electronic invoice, within 10 (ten) working days, payments according to the electronic invoice are made to Bolt's bank account (bank requisites are indicated in Article 4 of the Special Terms) by bank transfer. The Customer is only responsible for the payment for the Bolt services used by the User on behalf of the Customer and a service fee in the amount of 15% (fifteen percent) of the payment for these services.

{color:#4c9aff}PK: We cannot agree that the Customer will be obliged to pay for the services once it accepts the rides (as I understand this is the intention of the Customer). All services performed by Bolt will be available in the Business Portal and the Customer is obliged to pay for them according to clause 2.5. Additionally, we cannot state that the Customer is only responsible for Bolt Services or the Service Fee as there are some other payments under T&C that the Customer may be obliged to pay.{color}

