Hello team! This request was originally rejected by me because of lack of the legal basis for sharing personal data, since the requester did not provide the link to acts or laws which obligate Bolt to assist the authorities and disclose the data. 
The list of approved valid legal bases applicable for Ukraine can be found [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/83887#list-of-legal-bases-applicable-in-different-countries]. 
The original request, however, refers to part 2 of Chapter 14 of [Law of Ukraine “On Protection of Personal Data”|https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/2297-17#Text]: *_Personal data dissemination without the consent of personal data subject or his authorised person is allowed in cases specified by law and only (if required) in the interests of national security, economic welfare and human rights._* 

[The Law of Ukraine “On Supporting the Functioning of the Ukrainian Language as the State Language“|https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/en/2704-19#Text] and chapters specified by the requester do not specify any obligation to share users' personal data. At the same time, part 8 of article 1 of this law define The Ukrainian language as a factor in the unity and _national security of Ukraine._ 

Taking this into account, we can consult with Privacy Legal team about the validity of this act for data disclosure, to determine if the wording "in the interests of national security"  is applicable for us in this case.

Our main concern is to provide a clear explanation of work of our platform, since the requester mentions, that Bolt Operations Ukraine provides transportation services and is an employer for drivers (and particular driver mentioned in this request), which is not true. Every data request we process is answered with an important clarification which I suggest to use in this case:

{color:#006644}The Bolt app is a technology that connects passengers with drivers to help them get around cities more efficiently.{color}

{color:#006644}The owner of the Bolt application is an Estonian company - Bolt Operations OÜ (limited liability company (registration code 14532901), established in the Republic of Estonia, address: Vana-Lõuna tn 15, Tallinn 10134, Estonia).{color}

{color:#006644}Use of the application in Ukraine is in accordance with the General Terms and Conditions for Passengers, Terms of Partnership for Drivers, Privacy Policy for Drivers and Privacy Policy for Passengers. In addition, the activities of Bolt Operations OÜ are governed by national Estonian law and EU law.{color}

In my opinion, after (and in case of) Privacy Legal approval, driver’s personal data should be disclosed with a note that Bolt Operations Ukraine does not provide transportation services and the driver, as a provider of transportation services (according to p. 1.6 of [General Terms for Fleet Partners / Drivers (effective from 20.11.2023)|https://bolt.eu/en-ua/legal/tnc-drivers/] is responsible for the supporting of the functioning of the Ukrainian Language as the State Language on his own.

